== Enemies ==
The '''Revelwood''', while introducing no new enemy factions, presents a more hostile and challenging environment than the Springlands. Many of the factions have been upgrade with new and more dangerous enemy variants, and the [[:c:Vukah|Vukah]] become the primary enemy faction for the first time in the '''Blackmire''' region.

[[:c:Scavenger|Scavengers]] are the first enemy faction encountered, having taken over the abandoned settlements in the south and west, including {{MapLink | icon= Village | WillowCrush | Willow Crush | size= 25px }}, {{MapLink | icon= Village | Thornhold | Thornhold | size= 25px }}, and {{MapLink | icon= Village | GlenwoodsEnd | Glenwood's End | size= 25px }}. Be wary of a new Scavenger variant dual wielding [[Acid Cleaver]]s patrolling these towns.

The [[:c:Fell|Fell]] are still present everywhere within the Shroud, but dominate the Shrouded areas in the east, particularly {{MapLink | icon= Village | PikemeadsReach | Pikemead's Reach | size= 25px }}. New Fell variants include the [[Fell Boar]] and the [[Fell Spitting Plant]], both good sources of {{item+iconright|Shroud Sack}}, and the heavily armored [[Fell Knight]]. 

The wildlife of the Revelwood are more exotic and deadly than their counterparts in the Springlands. There is one new tameable critter - the {{item+iconright|Fae Deer}} - found in both the Revelwood proper and the Blackmire. Another passive critter - the [[Mushroom Crab]] - is not tameable and will put up a considerable fight if attacked. Players in both areas should also expect to encounter aggressive packs of wild [[Boar]] roaming the forests, poisonous [[Spitting Plant]]s growing around mud pits, and [[Bat]]s and [[Spider]]s lurking in caves. Venturing into the Blackmire presents new dangers, including alligator-like [[Snapjaw]]s attacking out of mud and tar pits, [[Giant Wasp]]s patrolling the skies, and [[Wisp]]s that split into multiple hostile creatures.

The [[:c:Vukah|Vukah]] are the only enemy faction missing from the Revelwood proper, but they more than make up for it by being the most prominent enemy faction of the Blackmire. The new Vukah, while not as challenging as the new Scavengers or Fell, including a spear-throwing variant and a heavily armored variant wearing a large skull mask. 

Finally, the [[:c:Hollow|Hollow]] are again rare outside the {{MapLink | icon= Hollow Halls | HollowHalls-Revelwood | Revelwood Hollow Halls | size= 25px }}. They can be found in {{MapLink | icon= Tomb | HiddenHollowTomb | Hidden Hollow Tomb | size= 25px }} and a few abandoned ruins scattered around the Revelwood, but not in the Blackmire.

